# The default data_dir. Everything the running app writes lands here -
# the autonomy journal, closed trades, the equity curve, report state and the
# generated reports. All of it is machine-specific runtime output, and the
# journals and equity curve carry real account balances, so none of it belongs
# in the repository.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash so it matches ONLY the data_dir at the repo
# root. Unanchored, git applies it at every level, which silently excluded
# src/qat/data/ and tests/data/ - the entire market-data layer was missing from
# the repository while the working tree looked clean.
/data/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# Office lock/temp files
~$*

# Claude Code local settings (machine-specific permission state)
.claude/settings.local.json

